===== path p incept
Incept a Toolpath document into a harness's on-disk session layout (file/stdin-shaped sibling of `export <provider>`)

Usage: path p incept [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  claude  Incept a Toolpath document into a Claude Code session layout
  cursor  Incept a Toolpath document into a Cursor (IDE) composer in `state.vscdb`
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --pretty
          Pretty-print JSON output

      --picker <PICKER>
          Backend for the interactive fuzzy picker used by `share`, `resume`, and `p import <provider>`. `auto` (default) uses the embedded skim picker and falls back to external `fzf` only when skim isn't compiled in; a hint is printed if `fzf` is also on PATH. `fzf`/`skim` force one backend and error if it isn't available

          Possible values:
          - auto: Pick whichever backend is available; prefer the embedded skim picker and fall back to external `fzf` when skim isn't compiled in. When external `fzf` is also on `PATH`, a one-time hint is printed to stderr advising `--picker fzf` for users who want their fzf config / keybindings
          - fzf:  Force the external `fzf` binary. Errors if it isn't on `PATH`
          - skim: Force the embedded skim picker. Errors if path-cli was built with `--no-default-features`
          
          [default: auto]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
===== path p incept claude
Incept a Toolpath document into a Claude Code session layout

Usage: path p incept claude [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -i, --input <INPUT>
          Input toolpath document (JSON path, cache id, or `-` for stdin). Reads stdin when omitted

  -p, --project <PROJECT>
          Target project directory. Defaults to the current directory when neither --project nor --output is given

  -o, --output <OUTPUT>
          Output JSONL to this file. Mutually exclusive with --project

      --pretty
          Pretty-print JSON output

      --picker <PICKER>
          Backend for the interactive fuzzy picker used by `share`, `resume`, and `p import <provider>`. `auto` (default) uses the embedded skim picker and falls back to external `fzf` only when skim isn't compiled in; a hint is printed if `fzf` is also on PATH. `fzf`/`skim` force one backend and error if it isn't available

          Possible values:
          - auto: Pick whichever backend is available; prefer the embedded skim picker and fall back to external `fzf` when skim isn't compiled in. When external `fzf` is also on `PATH`, a one-time hint is printed to stderr advising `--picker fzf` for users who want their fzf config / keybindings
          - fzf:  Force the external `fzf` binary. Errors if it isn't on `PATH`
          - skim: Force the embedded skim picker. Errors if path-cli was built with `--no-default-features`
          
          [default: auto]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
===== path p incept cursor
Incept a Toolpath document into a Cursor (IDE) composer in `state.vscdb`

Usage: path p incept cursor [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -i, --input <INPUT>
          Input toolpath document (JSON path, cache id, or `-` for stdin). Reads stdin when omitted

  -p, --project <PROJECT>
          Target workspace folder. Defaults to the current directory when neither --project nor --output is given

  -o, --output <OUTPUT>
          Output the projected `CursorSession` as pretty JSON to this file. Mutually exclusive with --project

      --pretty
          Pretty-print JSON output

      --picker <PICKER>
          Backend for the interactive fuzzy picker used by `share`, `resume`, and `p import <provider>`. `auto` (default) uses the embedded skim picker and falls back to external `fzf` only when skim isn't compiled in; a hint is printed if `fzf` is also on PATH. `fzf`/`skim` force one backend and error if it isn't available

          Possible values:
          - auto: Pick whichever backend is available; prefer the embedded skim picker and fall back to external `fzf` when skim isn't compiled in. When external `fzf` is also on `PATH`, a one-time hint is printed to stderr advising `--picker fzf` for users who want their fzf config / keybindings
          - fzf:  Force the external `fzf` binary. Errors if it isn't on `PATH`
          - skim: Force the embedded skim picker. Errors if path-cli was built with `--no-default-features`
          
          [default: auto]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
